{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> The one speaking, or the reader, or the herald:" "<b>Pave, pave.</b> The highway, clear it of stone. And the reason for the doubling is that the caller calls thus, one time after another:" "<b>The way of my people.</b> For they were servants of HaShem; therefore at the end of the passage: there is no peace, said YHWH to the wicked."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {2 "Resolved יי as YHWH; Ibn Ezra's text likely has the divine name abbreviated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:58.084301948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}